    an_limits:'MusicXML (.musicxml, .xml or compressed .mxl) keeps the source notation. MIDI is rebuilt as notation on the rhythm grid you choose (1/16 by default); hands follow the MIDI tracks when they separate cleanly, otherwise a pitch split. A key signature in the file is kept; without one the key is estimated, and you can override it. A missing meter defaults to 4/4. Tempo changes are used for playback; repeats are not expanded. No PDF.', nav_analysis:'Score & analysis', an_title:'Score & analysis', an_desc:'Open a MIDI or MusicXML file, or start with an example. Select notes to study keys, chords and harmony. Everything stays on this device.', an_file:'Open file', an_hint:'Click a note or an empty spot in a bar · Shift extends · drag to select', an_clear:'Clear selection', an_play:'Play selection', an_chord:'Chord', an_none:'No exact match', an_minor:'minor', an_major:'major', an_tip:'Keys are estimated with duration-weighted Krumhansl–Kessler profiles, so a major key and its relative minor are told apart; the fit value r shows how clearly the notes match. Chords are matched beat by beat against chord templates weighted by duration, so passing notes lower the confidence instead of breaking the match. Roman numerals follow the written or chosen key. Click a chord or motif to select its notes.',
